[
    {
        "id": "the-first-computer",
        "title": "The First Encounter with Silicon",
        "date": "2026-01-25",
        "sections": [
            {
                "heading": "The Box",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "It was 1998 when the beige box first arrived. It hummed with a promise of worlds I hadn't yet imagined."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "heading": "The Screen",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "image",
                        "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1547082299-de196ea013d6",
                        "caption": "The glow of the CRT monitor was my first guide."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "I spent hours watching the cursor blink, waiting for the courage to type something that mattered."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "train-to-nowhere",
        "title": "The Train to Nowhere",
        "date": "2025-11-12",
        "sections": [
            {
                "heading": "Departure",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "We boarded the night train in heavy rain. The windows were streaked with city lights dissolving into water. There was no destination in mind, just the act of leaving."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "heading": "Transit",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "At 3 AM, the train stopped in a field. No station, no lights. Just absolute darkness and the sound of the engine idling."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "image",
                        "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1474487548417-781cb71495f3",
                        "caption": "Waiting in the dark."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "internet-died",
        "title": "The Day the Internet Died",
        "date": "2025-08-04",
        "sections": [
            {
                "heading": "The Cut",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "A backhoe three streets over severed the main fiber line. The cafe went silent. It was a fascinating sociological experiment."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "heading": "The Aftermath",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "People looked up. They looked at each other. For two hours, we were returned to 1995. I spoke to a stranger about coffee beans."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "Then the connection returned, and heads bowed back down in unison, like prayer."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "building-the-cabin",
        "title": "Building the Cabin",
        "date": "2025-06-20",
        "sections": [
            {
                "heading": "Foundation",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "Digging holes for posts is humbling work. The earth pushes back. Every rock is an argument you have to win with a shovel."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "heading": "Framing",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "image",
                        "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1449247613801-be00129558ee",
                        "caption": "The skeleton of the structure."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "When the first wall went up, it changed from 'a pile of wood' to 'a place'. Space was enclosed. It was primitive magic."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "lost-year",
        "title": "The Lost Year",
        "date": "2024-01-01",
        "sections": [
            {
                "heading": "Burnout",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "I didn't realize I was burnt out until I tried to write an email and stared at the screen for forty minutes. My brain had simply refused to render the interface."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "heading": "Recovery",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "I spent the year doing everything except what I was good at. I painted poorly. I cooked questionable meals. I walked without a GPS."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "Slowly, the color returned to the world."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "id": "crossing-ocean",
        "title": "Crossing the Ocean",
        "date": "2023-09-15",
        "sections": [
            {
                "heading": "The Flight",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "14 hours over the Pacific. The dateline is a strange concept—you lose a day and gain it back, or lose it forever. Time becomes fluid."
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "heading": "Landing",
                "content": [
                    {
                        "type": "image",
                        "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1436491865332-7a61a109cc05",
                        "caption": "Above the clouds."
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "text": "Touching down in a country where you don't speak the language is the ultimate reset. You are a child again. You have to point and smile to survive."
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
]